      "Original bug: q was set from the k smallest elements (sorted_indices[:k]) instead of the k-th largest, and t was initialized only for top-k elements, so middle elements with x_i > q violated x_i <= t_i + q.",
      "Fix: q = min(x[top-k]) and t = max(0, x - q) for all elements; diff changes idx_of_smallest slice from sorted_indices[:k] to sorted_indices[:-k].",
